messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: pngget.c
Line: 1130
Function: png_get_PLTE
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: When PNG_INFO_PLTE is set and 'palette' is non-NULL, the function unconditionally writes to '*num_palette' without checking if 'num_palette' is NULL. A caller requesting only the palette (passing num_palette == NULL) will trigger a NULL pointer dereference at '*num_palette = info_ptr->num_palette;'.

Source context:
```c
